BINARY=/tmp/gxopus_lunaabs/gxemul
PLANTED -- each slot disassembled and checked against the emulator's own spelling:
  0x00010000 word=0x24850000 dis='st\tr4,r5,0x0'      OK
  0x00010004 word=0x14850000 dis='ld\tr4,r5,0x0'      OK
  0x00010008 word=0x24860000 dis='st\tr4,r6,0x0'      OK
  0x0001000c word=0x14860000 dis='ld\tr4,r6,0x0'      OK
C1 LIVENESS -- plain RAM through the same decode:
  C1 RAM readback                                                got=0x12345678 want=0x12345678 OK
LUNAABS_ROW=live       RESULT=OK        
C2 DEVICE SIGNATURE -- MASK0: the handler's own >>8; RAM cannot produce this:
  C2 read INT_ST_MASK0 after write 0xfc000000                    got=0x00fc0000 want=0x00fc0000 OK
LUNAABS_ROW=devsig     RESULT=OK        
A1 ATTRIBUTION -- the SAME two-store sequence on the CONNECTED slot 0 must survive:
   MASK0 already holds 0xfc000000 (bit 26 set); store 1 to SOFT_INT0 -> reassert -> slot 0 asserts
  A1 SOFT_INT0 readback (the stored 1; read clears it)           got=0x00000001 want=0x00000001 OK
LUNAABS_ROW=slot0      RESULT=OK        
A2 THE MASK1 STORE ALONE -- arms the ABSENT slot 1; no pending bit yet, must survive:
LUNAABS_ROW=mask1      RESULT=OK        MASK1 readback 0x00fc0000 (as-is => 0x00fc0000 in 23..0; a decline => 0)
W1 THE WITNESS -- SOFT_INT1 store: slot 1's bit 26 becomes pending, enable has it, irqActive clear
   -> INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d->cpu_irq[1]) through a NULL interrupt_assert on a one-cpu machine
LUNAABS_ROW=soft1      RESULT=OK        survived; SOFT_INT1 readback 0x00000001
C3 LIVENESS AGAIN -- the machine still executes:
  C3 RAM readback                                                got=0x0badf00d want=0x0badf00d OK
LUNAABS_ROW=live2      RESULT=OK        
LUNA_ABSENTCPU_WITNESS=PASS
LUNAABS_RESULT=6/6
PROBE_WALL=0.6s
